#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192335 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Three-Variable Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "89d0136d-63d1-540b-a3be-acff2d0bbbb5" :question/math-academy-id "e-11027" :question/problem "For the function  $g(x,y,z) = 2 (x + 1)e^z+ yz,$  evaluate  $\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial z}$ at $(1,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2(x+1){e}^{z}+yz) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2(x+1){e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & =2(x+1)\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & =2(x+1){e}^{z}+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1,1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z}{|}_{(1,1,1)} & =2(1+1){e}^{1}+1 \\\\  & =4e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192336 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "0fd784a0-5146-5f7b-9936-8d3bc43d7062" :question/math-academy-id "e-11028" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ for $f(x,y) =x^2y\\ln{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & =y\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =y\\cdot ((2x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})) \\\\  & =y(2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x) \\\\  & =xy(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192341 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "fc8ba431-5a97-5f57-9a83-fdcf4ac98d39" :question/math-academy-id "e-11048" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) =\\ln(y-x^2),$ evaluate $f_x(1,9).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-{x}^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (y\\cdot 0-2x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,9)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,9) & =-\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{9-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192345 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Quotient Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "6f7bdbcf-fb8e-5c70-b368-4e73cc94bdb2" :question/math-academy-id "e-11112" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{4x-y}{x+y^2},$ evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4x-y}{x+{y}^{2}}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x-y)\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2})}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot 1}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4x+4{y}^{2}-4x+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{2}+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(2,-1)} & =\\frac{4(-1)^{2}+(-1)}{{(2+{(-1)}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Three-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a7efc43-d3ce-53aa-b521-0885aded7a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320194} {:answer/id #uuid "15e881f3-118c-5fd3-a368-060757825e0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320195} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7e62a2-9fc6-5910-b7b9-e15d9a9e860c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320196} {:answer/id #uuid "54616207-a198-5962-9f81-131b777e1962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320197} {:answer/id #uuid "0d36358e-a40f-5cac-8f14-41e4aad501e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d36358e-a40f-5cac-8f14-41e4aad501e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320198} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc6ea07-0fa3-5626-8a44-e35219654958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "adb985bd-dcb3-5be8-a084-1d0889512850" :question/math-academy-id "q-132253" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(3,-1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}{({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})}^{-1/2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}) & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{z}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot (2x+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(3,-1,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(3,-1,-2)} & =\\frac{(3)(-1)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+4(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9+16}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e287542-a75c-5c22-bbb5-c406a76e87b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320201} {:answer/id #uuid "11caa765-db5e-562d-8949-2d15235e8758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320202} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d05e49-de30-5a20-9b84-75fa8d64a8f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320203} {:answer/id #uuid "23b0bbd3-2469-5dba-b867-9982d62ddcbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{2y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320204} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb29826-414c-58bc-af2e-da23d2cb0e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11caa765-db5e-562d-8949-2d15235e8758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320202} :answer-field/id #uuid "a355a4ea-1b10-5d8e-a146-28a6f0966803" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5b2ae4a-57b2-54a4-b907-816f60555712" :question/math-academy-id "q-159656" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}y}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot y\\cdot 2x-y\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5158365-736d-563f-9720-a896581a716d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2x\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320208} {:answer/id #uuid "d75894c6-0b46-526c-beea-084d2b197067" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320209} {:answer/id #uuid "d1877610-3f44-5502-9c47-bb4b9838754c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320210} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5aac6c-fdcb-58d5-af3b-3cda85568fff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320211} {:answer/id #uuid "39662ffe-3427-5f74-b509-385d247ec294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1877610-3f44-5502-9c47-bb4b9838754c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320210} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1c2334f-bd50-569a-bb66-6ebffa35318c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84882c75-fbb0-5e5f-ad0e-928900017882" :question/math-academy-id "q-159658" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{2xy-1}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum and the constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-1) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}(2x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot (2x\\cdot 1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "488422f0-c3e5-5c7e-868f-203325676aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320215} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ee3f0e-e153-5075-82e1-f6a246bdc922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320216} {:answer/id #uuid "570e2a01-6a95-527e-9b80-c01e84878a4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320217} {:answer/id #uuid "68107968-0b55-53bf-a708-735e997826be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320218} {:answer/id #uuid "2f6ea151-d148-579e-98e9-8a5857ca2c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68107968-0b55-53bf-a708-735e997826be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320218} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd36a4f6-1d5e-54ce-be34-89b01ecdb987" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cf8e1bf-4d61-5043-9e78-9d1d07ae32ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-159660" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot (2x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2) & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}+2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2\\pi +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi +2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c7679d-ffe0-50d3-97db-0a1b7cbdb0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320222} {:answer/id #uuid "d0fe4f1e-f8f3-53dc-9103-6cee3e737266" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320223} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c53be7-bdbd-5954-934b-b4a21d167629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320224} {:answer/id #uuid "2c11682d-984b-546b-bbca-cf94ac6506d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320225} {:answer/id #uuid "23e79b07-95ef-5d34-b6ed-e46b3a157e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7c53be7-bdbd-5954-934b-b4a21d167629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320224} :answer-field/id #uuid "33ea1e05-94a1-505c-9621-87f953291990" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf13512e-3387-5291-88a0-4f86e5763eb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-159700" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}{{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,\\pi /2)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-0}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7281c65f-e044-521a-a051-59324b55df69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320229} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b663cf-2c6b-5a52-b15c-a31438f539e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320230} {:answer/id #uuid "48c55673-9ed6-571b-8182-6f2df9653f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320231} {:answer/id #uuid "47f1c1d7-8a96-5058-ae6d-1bc793bffb0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320232} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7f292e-b10a-5a2d-b4a2-407df8c9ae72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7281c65f-e044-521a-a051-59324b55df69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320229} :answer-field/id #uuid "03fef776-b21c-52e7-a3c9-ffea0fe6a3c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8a7e486-17de-592f-96c1-9311ddc05fcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-159709" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(0,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(0,2)} & =\\frac{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-0\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+0}{(2+0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a560833b-667b-5026-aa1b-a1b70d1b97c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320236} {:answer/id #uuid "44ce801d-ad4f-58ec-a264-d436b4b0a9f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320237} {:answer/id #uuid "c41a924b-f2b1-5189-96b2-61bbc57a1a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320238} {:answer/id #uuid "872afa34-b9d5-5d1f-b6a9-43b0753e333c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320239} {:answer/id #uuid "85c9243f-2447-5aa8-b59a-d7f19a7d209a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c9243f-2447-5aa8-b59a-d7f19a7d209a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320240} :answer-field/id #uuid "a68bbd05-c360-5161-b3fb-6b7b3f22bb66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b4241fc-d343-57db-b682-2b4f5e3dcd59" :question/math-academy-id "q-159713" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x+y)\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x+y})}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y))}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot 1)}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6(x+y)-(3x+y)}{2\\sqrt{x+y}})}{x+y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x+5y}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=3x+5y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b6dc98b-68dd-5072-906d-8b9e815d01ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320243} {:answer/id #uuid "97175546-a10b-5ab1-a4e3-c93cb254f0fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320244} {:answer/id #uuid "95f5ba68-f7b1-5df8-99c1-7d6af7dfd5b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320245} {:answer/id #uuid "7557c234-b64f-5733-9a53-ee2f280c8be3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320246} {:answer/id #uuid "52f329d9-dbc8-5ed9-bd77-fb5bd56924c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+{x}^{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95f5ba68-f7b1-5df8-99c1-7d6af7dfd5b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320245} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd28b765-22d3-59ad-8b30-b58121413eab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "360572a0-aaba-5b94-9db4-07a54f0fa3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-159714" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{2h(x,y)}{{x}^{3}y}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot 2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{3}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=1-x{y}^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9100cb77-e0d2-59d4-94ab-8d24a15761ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320250} {:answer/id #uuid "e9728124-f97b-5a9b-acad-a73f18baaba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320251} {:answer/id #uuid "13f2aca9-b9d3-5196-867b-f272808766a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320252} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7b1e74-5e2b-553c-b055-29033c86538e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320253} {:answer/id #uuid "6bbe01f4-528b-5d33-a90a-8d9ac2571b14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bbe01f4-528b-5d33-a90a-8d9ac2571b14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320254} :answer-field/id #uuid "067f38fd-0d37-5f3d-8fff-7a7d824c10f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "068ab429-8193-5817-9f73-d6ab1bfc151f" :question/math-academy-id "q-159716" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)={x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x{y}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))-{y}^{3}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =((4{x}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x))-{y}^{3} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "435df410-881b-58de-be34-afbbeb798f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2x+y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320257} {:answer/id #uuid "9e471127-6f76-5680-8bc2-db366149adb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320258} {:answer/id #uuid "e3733ea0-3278-579d-843c-17a435db6857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320259} {:answer/id #uuid "af57bbc0-a7d0-59e2-be79-1ed441456dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320260} {:answer/id #uuid "80884e48-5e32-528e-998e-36d63b7ecacc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af57bbc0-a7d0-59e2-be79-1ed441456dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320260} :answer-field/id #uuid "57441ed7-c123-5db0-9d04-b69822dfdf07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da6991b3-2060-51f5-9aca-09e2d4207eb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-159723" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{y}^{2})}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (-2y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{y}^{3}+2{x}^{2}y+2{y}^{3}}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy+2{x}^{2}y}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1+x)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=2xy(1+x).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5cbe4e7-0b60-5240-8c81-37ca3e825df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190994} {:answer/id #uuid "ecad333e-15c6-5795-811d-950b822f9ddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190995} {:answer/id #uuid "f26c6cb2-0e72-596d-97ab-61be3ea29a96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190996} {:answer/id #uuid "537c32f3-aaef-5c54-baf2-f06eabb90d42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190997} {:answer/id #uuid "667e4592-59e8-5fb2-aeef-533cd0c37555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5cbe4e7-0b60-5240-8c81-37ca3e825df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190994} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc79c67f-1245-5bb4-8883-fdf9baee5a43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d20c624a-1709-5495-88ea-45d0df97ea34" :question/math-academy-id "q-159751" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product, the chain, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot {e}^{xy}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy}))-{x}^{2}\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot {e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy))-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =({e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y))-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =({e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot 1)-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}-2{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & ={e}^{1\\cdot 1}+1\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 1}-2\\cdot {1}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =e+e-2 \\\\  & =2e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320262 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3086d83d-61bb-59e7-b185-643aeb330f80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320264} {:answer/id #uuid "94095686-fb03-5489-8d44-ed74c6110c86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320265} {:answer/id #uuid "9c12fa1d-6b4e-5d2f-ad17-20619c9aef19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320266} {:answer/id #uuid "14af26d2-5137-5aa6-bd3e-5e0137f114d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320267} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9b0047-327d-524d-a74c-ee9e3db6880a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3086d83d-61bb-59e7-b185-643aeb330f80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320264} :answer-field/id #uuid "f81703f5-6968-5d08-83d1-262086ef4abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3aac067-ce23-515b-b5c8-0d28c68fc2b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-159752" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\sqrt{y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product, the chain, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1+\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1/4,4)} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4)+1+\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263c67a4-1b69-51b0-8e49-99f1b62d6596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320271} {:answer/id #uuid "e5087c73-7cfe-5e82-b3d7-bcc2bd0d9d9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320272} {:answer/id #uuid "2b013f7d-6b9d-52fa-a67d-131252d6bde1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320273} {:answer/id #uuid "80e995c1-7f73-5e90-81d9-ee1596f15b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320274} {:answer/id #uuid "b73e783a-b5f2-5297-b4fe-4124eccb1bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80e995c1-7f73-5e90-81d9-ee1596f15b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320274} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec92e6d8-b395-5680-8f28-95e0b23dd36f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "834163bd-4e3f-5a32-83f7-f9500712f022" :question/math-academy-id "q-159766" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(2,\\sqrt{5}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain, the sum, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) & =1\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot 0+2y) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\sqrt{5}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\sqrt{5})} & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}+\\frac{{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+5}+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{4+5}} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e960f6d1-5006-5ddc-ada2-59b46924bf73" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30dbb420-483f-5d1f-a7d3-a2f4b602a962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320278} {:answer/id #uuid "afe3e5cf-2b48-5630-9e1b-e16dbe2b475a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320279} {:answer/id #uuid "8cef5789-eced-5f56-b32e-efb38dc3e40f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320280} {:answer/id #uuid "94a3c8a4-8b8a-5daa-9abe-1a69a4a1d7c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320281} {:answer/id #uuid "45b8d6cb-eafa-56d9-a0ed-1ad007dead4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe3e5cf-2b48-5630-9e1b-e16dbe2b475a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320279} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a03980-1c6a-5c4e-9bd4-6bbd7ae57d71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f954155-7c22-5e6e-a4d1-3429c98b0a35" :question/math-academy-id "q-159768" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(2,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & =x(\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =x(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\pi )} & =2\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =2(-1-\\pi \\cdot 0)+(-1) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Three-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a519aa6b-39eb-575b-b283-6f37d060353c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191671} {:answer/id #uuid "ac55263c-1d2d-59da-a5f0-7ab71511aba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191672} {:answer/id #uuid "06f0bef4-3f30-5fd3-aad6-983c129d61de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191673} {:answer/id #uuid "13c377d3-0475-5865-82c3-30718bbe05a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191674} {:answer/id #uuid "5d345158-c661-5040-83d2-c3bdc27adccc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13c377d3-0475-5865-82c3-30718bbe05a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191674} :answer-field/id #uuid "57747ca4-beb2-53d9-a735-8032c35104a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3cd9c82e-fba1-518a-8285-94d9c7befa44" :question/math-academy-id "q-35710" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})-(0) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,0,1)} & =2(1)^{2}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a90859-36d7-5724-99d7-c7a175c77722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320285} {:answer/id #uuid "4967a27b-dcfa-5635-877f-57347de9a89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y(x+1)^{2y-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320286} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b07d9c-0271-5c5e-9ba5-7447f26e22b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320287} {:answer/id #uuid "cab8a909-340a-5940-8d09-02fc459e24a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320288} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c04959-279e-589e-8fe6-d8416de9f250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10a90859-36d7-5724-99d7-c7a175c77722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320285} :answer-field/id #uuid "45fed4a4-b3ae-5a1b-a914-62c399e435a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320284}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcac2fd7-4ed3-57e6-9593-aacaa7508a58" :question/math-academy-id "q-35713" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)=(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x+1)^{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+1) & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot (1+0) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14cc6590-c2fd-5395-9481-0e5c0d9b8b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "986ab1d8-c1d0-58ef-bace-b81132cb4886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191677} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf4dc6f-c84a-5136-83ec-c5ca49d08da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191678} {:answer/id #uuid "37cdf34a-abee-5df2-96ca-1e9dbe9d190f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191679} {:answer/id #uuid "70e039c0-0f1c-5c22-b107-6bacd01f0c46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191680} {:answer/id #uuid "710a0ad2-7f20-52d4-9c39-9154017c9eec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37cdf34a-abee-5df2-96ca-1e9dbe9d190f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191679} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3a5438b-5884-580c-9063-4baff8a1528a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "52ec8ecc-7425-5715-9001-87fc8bd443a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-35718" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}y,$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y) & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)+{x}^{2}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =x{e}^{xy}\\cdot (1)+{x}^{2} \\\\  & =x{e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Three-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ce38b5-5a75-546e-8286-4537895fb589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320292} {:answer/id #uuid "c0541915-547b-5738-9c8b-c4e026b5a12f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z-(z+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320293} {:answer/id #uuid "feeadf0d-b352-541f-8bde-48ef85847b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320294} {:answer/id #uuid "6cbc9ef1-ff62-5892-b411-81f4c7566911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320295} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8c69f2-94af-542c-873a-e94551e3f14e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7ce38b5-5a75-546e-8286-4537895fb589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320292} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4168855-2873-5868-b164-a249883a4198" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "191a6c22-e38e-5a60-a84b-fb853e195152" :question/math-academy-id "q-35721" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{z}(x,y,z)$ for $g(x,y,z)=(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}((z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(z+y) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Three-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a62b068-ead1-5e8e-a97e-283c9c03776d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320299} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1faa4d-aeb3-5a96-b91c-063b7e03c2f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320300} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b5115a-13ea-5805-9e42-7c6cde8ffeca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320301} {:answer/id #uuid "bf5512d5-5fe2-558b-b20e-81f457504cd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320302} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2b07b4-71a7-582e-8934-41bddaed16d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5b5115a-13ea-5805-9e42-7c6cde8ffeca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320301} :answer-field/id #uuid "cddf011a-baa1-5f8d-b037-db8d60d27eac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d80f449c-f2b6-559b-a95b-ee208f9e4649" :question/math-academy-id "q-64907" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=xyz-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(1,0,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot 1-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}yz-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) & =yz-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz) \\\\  & =yz-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)\\cdot (z) \\\\  & =yz-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz) \\\\  & =z(y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1,0,\\pi )} & =\\pi (0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi (0-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5cebc16-84c3-5ec8-b1f1-5f9c51a69d94" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Partial Derivatives of Three-Variable Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc7cff8b-277b-53c5-8064-b15a1d07a4e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320306} {:answer/id #uuid "4c88c154-868a-5769-9973-b30fdaa8e13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320307} {:answer/id #uuid "afd0e988-1ddc-5407-b45c-5e8d4a7bddfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320308} {:answer/id #uuid "5e666248-9d96-5d9e-ab1c-74de23ef882f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320309} {:answer/id #uuid "016c3b28-8204-5023-8aa6-a51db3e81287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "016c3b28-8204-5023-8aa6-a51db3e81287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320310} :answer-field/id #uuid "13d82bc1-c010-56e4-aa2a-21c043b106dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "526dd47f-a660-5cfc-b389-d90165c8c680" :question/math-academy-id "q-86812" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}{e}^{xy}-{y}^{2}{e}^{yz},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}$ at the point $(0,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}{e}^{xy}-{y}^{2}{e}^{yz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}{e}^{xy})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}{e}^{yz}) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})-{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{yz})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})-{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{yz}) & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot 2z-{y}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{yz}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot 2z-{y}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{yz}\\cdot y \\\\  & =2z{e}^{xy}-{y}^{3}{e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z}{|}_{(0,-1,1)} & =2(1){e}^{(0)(-1)}-(-1)^{3}{e}^{(-1)(1)} \\\\  & =2+{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
